"name":"Solitude","facility":"Dormitory","eliteLevel":"Elite 1","description":"When this Operator is assigned to a Dormitory, self Morale recovered +0.7 per hour"}],"modules":[{"type":"Original","name":"Estelle's Badge","stages":[]},{"type":"Upgrade","name":"CEN-Y: Farewell Gifts from the Wildlands","mission":{"requirement1":"Complete a total of 5 battles; You must deploy your own Estelle, and have Estelle deal at least 12,000 damage","requirement2":"Clear Main Theme 7-4 with a 3-star rating; You must deploy your own Estelle, and have Estelle defeat at least 15 enemies"},"stages":[{"stage":"Stage 1","attributesIncreased":"HP +70 , ATK +32","effectLabel":"New trait","effectText":"While above 50% HP, reduces the amount of Physical damage taken by 20%","cost":[{"name":"Module Data Block","quantity":1},{"name":"Coagulating Gel","quantity":4},{"name":"LMD","quantity":20000}]},{"stage":"Stage 2","attributesIncreased":"HP +100 , ATK +43","effectLabel":"Self-Healing improved","effectText":"Restores 14% of Max HP whenever an enemy is defeated in the surrounding 8 tiles","cost":[{"name":"Module Data Block","quantity":1},{"name":"Data Supplement Stick","quantity":15},{"name":"Integrated Device","quantity":5},{"name":"LMD","quantity":25000}]},{"stage":"Stage 3","attributesIncreased":"HP +120 , ATK +52","effectLabel":"Self-Healing improved","effectText":"Restores 16% of Max HP whenever an enemy is defeated in the surrounding 8 tiles","cost":[{"name":"Module Data Block","quantity":1},{"name":"Data Supplement Instrument","quantity":5},{"name":"Loxic Kohl","quantity":6},{"name":"LMD","quantity":30000}]}]}],"review":{"official":"Estelle, her infection only at a moderate stage, attracted attention due to mutations triggered by\nOripathy\n. She later sought medical asylum at\nRhodes Island\nafter trying several other treatment programs.\nShe received psychological counseling and a battery of examinations with her consent before officially joining Rhodes Island as a guard with a squad of\noperators\n.","editor":null,"rating":null},"synergies":[],"techniques":[{"technique":null,"techniqueDescription":null,"description":null}],"guides":[],"stats":{"phases":[{"elite":0,"minLevel":1,"maxLevel":45,"base":{"hp":1140,"atk":278,"def":133,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":18,"block":2,"interval":1.2},"max":{"hp":1462,"atk":387,"def":190,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":18,"block":2,"interval":1.2},"rangeId":"1-1"},{"elite":1,"minLevel":1,"maxLevel":60,"base":{"hp":1462,"atk":387,"def":190,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":20,"block":2,"interval":1.2},"max":{"hp":1875,"atk":524,"def":258,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":20,"block":2,"interval":1.2},"rangeId":"1-1"},{"elite":2,"minLevel":1,"maxLevel":70,"base":{"hp":1875,"atk":524,"def":258,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":22,"block":3,"interval":1.2},"max":{"hp":2500,"atk":690,"def":315,"res":0,"redeploy":70,"dp":22,"block":3,"interval":1.2},"rangeId":"1-1"}],"trust":{"hp":350,"atk":0,"def":0}},"files":[{"section":"Clinical Analysis","unlock":"Unlocked at 25 trust","description":"Imaging tests for this Operator showed blurry outlines of internal organs with visible dark spots. Unusually high concentrations of Originium particles were present in her circulatory system, indicating infection and confirming her as Infected at this stage. \n\n[Cell-Originium Assimilation] 16% \nSevere mutation following infection, sprouting horns noncharacteristic to the race. Close observation recommended. \n\n[Blood Originium-Crystal Density] 0.31u/L \nInfection entering mid-stage, tests required to discern specific effects. \n\n[Mutation Assessment] \nBased on current observations of Archosauria, double horns are not an expected racial trait. According to Operator Estelle's own account, she has never had any manifestation of biological mutations growing up. Thus, the mutated horns are determined to be caused by Oripathy."},{"section":"Archive File 1","unlock":"Unlocked at 25 trust","description":"Operator Estelle is habitually nervous and self-restrained, constantly in a state of unease, though most Operators have paid little attention to her state of mind. Estelle's two mutant horns are the primary cause of her worried behavior. \nIn the past, Estelle has slipped into depression over the mutation and withdrawn from all social activity. It is advised that the Doctor provide further psychological counseling to prevent total self-isolation."},{"section":"Archive File 2","unlock":"Unlocked at 100 trust","description":"Despite her typical baseline level of anxiety, Estelle has never appeared nervous in battle. Observations have shown that she retains her Archosaurian warrior spirit, as is present in Gavial, a fellow Archosaurian. Estelle possesses remarkable melee combat abilities, employing her own body as her primary weapon. Her enormous horns and powerful tail have won her many a victory, as she charges mightily ahead, driven by bestial instinct. \nHer fellow operators have stood in awe of her ferocity. To which Estelle responds with uncharacteristic withdrawal, opting for solo combat and giving her teammates a wide berth, focusing only on her commander's orders."},{"section":"Archive File 3","unlock":"Unlocked at 150 trust","description":"Currently, Rhodes Island has established a series of special arrangements for Operator Estelle, including psychological evaluation and disease management. Due to Estelle's expression of a strong desire to recover, it is best to avoid explaining the situation to her for the time being. \nBased upon current medical technology, the prospects of containing Estelle's Oripathy are more realistic. Monitoring of the patient's psychological condition has shown that she is more willing to 'accept the disease as a part of her and live in a non-human form,' which is a positive development. However, it is possible that this will be a source of instability in the future. \nBased upon this assessment, the relevant personnel will must continue to evaluate and adjust their methods in order to actively guide Estelle to proper self-acknowledgement."}]},"appearances":[{"label":"Base","iconPath":"/four-star-icons/Estelle%20-%20Base.webp","fullPath":"/four-star-skins/Estelle%20-%20Base.webp"},{"label":"Elite 2","iconPath":"/four-star-icons/Estelle%20-%20Elite%202.webp","fullPath":"/four-star-skins/Estelle%20-%20Elite%202.webp"},{"label":"La Valse Couronnée de Fleurs","iconPath":"/four-star-icons/Estelle%20-%20La%20Valse%20Couronn%C3%A9e%20de%20Fleurs.webp","fullPath":"/four-star-skins/Estelle%20-%20La%20Valse%20Couronn%C3%A9e%20de%20Fleurs.webp"}],"skinObtainByLabel":{},"synergyMatches":[],"autoSynergyGroups":[{"name":"Sargon","type":"faction","entries":[{"operatorName":"Titi","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Titi%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":true,"badges":[{"label":"T2","skillIconPath":null,"talentLabel":"T2","sourceText":"Deployed [Minos] and [Sargon] Operators gain Vigor effect of +22 (+2) ASPD when HP is above 50%","matchedKeyword":"Sargon"}]},{"operatorName":"Carnelian","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Carnelian%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorName":"Eunectes","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Eunectes%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorName":"Gavial the Invincible","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Gavial%20the%20Invincible%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorName":"Mantra","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Mantra%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorName":"Narantuya","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Narantuya%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorName":"Passenger","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Passenger%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorName":"Pepe","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Pepe%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorName":"Pozëmka","operatorIconPath":"/six-star-icons/Poz%C3%ABmka%20-%20Base.webp","isContributor":false,"badges":[]},{"operatorN